Short:        Directory Opus 4.x file manager
Author:       Jonathan Potter, Jacek Rzeuski, Andrzej Rogozynski
Uploader:     Andrzej Rogozynski <@UPLOADER@>
Type:         biz/dopus
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     68020+
Kurz:         Directory Opus 4.x Dateimanager

Directory Opus 4 is the classic two-pane file manager by GP Software,
released under the GPL in 2000.  Jacek Rzeuski continued it up to 4.16
(biz/dopus/DOpus416JRbin.lha).  4.x carries on from there: the 4.16
sources, built with vbcc for the 68020 (no FPU needed), with bug fixes
and new features.  The ChangeLog below lists what has changed.

Installation
------------

Unpack the archive anywhere and start DirectoryOpus from the
DirectoryOpus4x drawer.  The drawer is self-contained:

  DirectoryOpus         the program
  Libs/dopus.library    found here, unless LIBS: has its own copy
  Modules/              ConfigOpus, DOpus_Disk, DOpus_Icon, DOpus_Print
  C/DOpusRT             runs commands for DOpus and waits for a key
  S/                    help files (English and translations)
  Catalogs/             deutsch, espanol, francais, italiano, polski, suomi

DirectoryOpus opens dopus.library from LIBS: first.  If an older
dopus.library is in LIBS:, delete it or replace it with the one in Libs/.
If one is already in memory, quit DirectoryOpus and run "avail flush".
The configuration files of 4.16 can be used as they are.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.0 or newer, 68020 or better.
- Optional: xadmaster.library, xfdmaster.library, powerpacker.library,
  popupmenu.library, screennotify.library, sysinfo.library, CyberGraphX,
  NewMouse wheel events.  DOpus uses them when they are installed.

